A:

Here's another way to do it.  This will work with any character and will return the substring that contains the character.  It's not particularly efficient, but it's straightforward.
public static String remove(String str, char c) {
    for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
        if (str.charAt(i) == c) {
            return str.substring(0, i) + str.substring(i + 1);
        }
    }
    return str;
}

